{"test":"text:nat_en.txt","n_prompt":113,"pp_s":9.509,"pp_ts":11.8840,"n_gen":128,"tg_ts":7.6758,"tg_total_ts":7.6477,"gen":"The wind came in the dark, and the sea was a black thing with white teeth. The lighthouse stood on the edge of the world, and the storm was a living thing, tearing at the stone walls, howling through the narrow windows. The keeper's hands were steady as he wrote, but his heart was a drum in his chest. He had seen storms before, but this was different. This was a storm that had a purpose.\nThe boat was supposed to come at dawn, but the sea had other plans. The keeper watched the waves crash against the rocks, and he thought of the men who had come before him,"}
